A noweb overlay over JSON (plan P3-22): each fragment name is one label token, whatever the grammar makes of the text around it.

```json(overlays: ["noweb"])
<<config>>=
{"name": "<<the name>>", "n": 1, <<more fields>>}
```

A rule turns it on for every JSON block; a CJK name keeps its bytes, and `<<` with no close on its line stays code:

#{ $.set({kind: 'codeblock', lang: 'json'}, {codeblock: {overlays: 'noweb'}}) }

```json
<<定义>>+=
{"a": [1, 2], "b": "x << y"}
```

An empty list switches it off again, and the same text is plain JSON:

#{ $.set({kind: 'codeblock', lang: 'json'}, {codeblock: {overlays: []}}) }

```json
<<定义>>+=
{"a": [1, 2]}
```
